issue.body:
### What happens

A `__cudnn$fusion` custom call is turned into a `kCustom` fusion in the pre-SPMD pipeline (`CuDnnCustomCallConverter`, `gpu_compiler.cc:686`), so unlike every other fusion it already exists at layout assignment.

`SetFusionLayouts` (`layout_assignment.cc:2473`) rewrites such a fusion's parameters and root, but deliberately preserves interior layouts for custom fusions. Nothing constrains the fusion's own layout to match that body, so as soon as layout assignment picks a non-default layout for the fusion the root disagrees with its own operands:

| | before layout assignment | after |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `%fusion` | `{2,1,0}` | `{1,0,2}` |
| ROOT `%multiply.0` | `{2,1,0}` | `{1,0,2}` (copied from the fusion) |
| `%dot.0` (interior) | `{2,1,0}` | `{2,1,0}` (untouched) |

```
RET_CHECK failure (xla/service/hlo_verifier.cc:4305) equal_predicate(result_layout, operand_layout)
Instruction shouldn't change layouts %multiply.0 = f32[2048,8,768]{1,0,2}
multiply(%dot.0, %Arg_2.0) From f32[2048,8,768]{1,0,2} To f32[2048,8,768]{2,1,0}
during context [end-of-post-layout_assignment]
```

The two tables above are read off `--xla_dump_to` dumps of a real training step, before and after the layout-assignment pass.

### Why not just clear the interior layouts

That is what ordinary fusions get, and it would make the verifier check inapplicable — but `cudnn_fusion_compiler` reads `minor_to_major` off those interior instructions (lines 246 and 540) to build the cuDNN graph, so they have to stay, and be consistent.

### Possible fix

Constrain the fusion instead, in `GpuLayoutAssignment::AddBackendConstraints` — the same shape as the `kRaggedDot` branch just above it:

```c++
} else if (HloPredicateIsOp<HloOpcode::kFusion>(instruction) &&
           instruction->fusion_kind() == HloInstruction::FusionKind::kCustom) {
  auto gpu_config = instruction->backend_config<GpuBackendConfig>();
  if (gpu_config.ok() &&
      gpu_config->fusion_backend_config().kind() == kCuDnnFusionKind) {
    for (int64_t i = 0; i < instruction->operand_count(); ++i) {
      Shape operand_shape = instruction->operand(i)->shape();
      LayoutUtil::SetToDefaultLayout(&operand_shape);
      TF_RETURN_IF_ERROR(SetOperandLayout(operand_shape, instruction, i));
    }
    Shape output_shape = instruction->shape();
    LayoutUtil::SetToDefaultLayout(&output_shape);
    TF_RETURN_IF_ERROR(SetInstructionLayout(output_shape, instruction));
  }
}
```

A copy outside the fusion is cheaper than an inconsistent body. This builds and clears the failure on a depth-12 training step; I have not measured what the copies cost, and there may well be a better constraint than "default layout".

Found alongside #48147 — this is the next failure once that one is fixed.
